---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Support — CodeWorksLabs" description="Find documentation, community help, issue reporting, and private contact routes for CodeWorksLabs products and services.">
  <section class="page-intro security-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Support</p>
    <h1>Start in the open.<br /><em>Route private matters carefully.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">Choose the route that matches the question. Visit the CodeWorksLabs forum for product discussions, updates and feature requests. For core DiscussionBridge support and discussion, use the DiscussionBridge forum. Private contact remains available when public discussion is inappropriate.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://docs.codeworkslabs.dev/">Browse documentation <span>↗</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://forum.codeworkslabs.dev/">Visit the CWL forum <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section security-grid">
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Community support</p>
      <h2>Ask, learn, and share</h2>
      <p>The CodeWorksLabs forum is a place for product discussions, updates, practical examples and feature requests. Share the problem you want to solve and the outcome you need. Planned and exploratory products are identified on their product pages.</p>
      <div class="text-links">
        <a class="text-link" href="https://forum.codeworkslabs.dev/c/general/4">Join the discussion →</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://forum.codeworkslabs.dev/t/discourse-network-by-cwl-plans-updates-and-your-use-cases/17">Discourse Network plans and use cases →</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Product help</p>
      <h2>Get help with a product</h2>
      <p>Choose the product you're using. Start with its documentation, then use its issue or support link if you still need help.</p>
      <div class="text-links">
        <a class="text-link" href="https://docs.codeworkslabs.dev/brand-navigation/">Brand Navigation documentation →</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/CodeWorksLabs/brand-navigation/issues">Brand Navigation issues →</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://forum.discussionbridge.dev/">DiscussionBridge forum →</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://discussionbridge.dev/support/">DiscussionBridge support →</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section platform-proof">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Direct contact</p><h2>Some conversations should not be public.</h2></div>
    <div><p class="large-copy">For private project, hosting, or implementation questions, contact CodeWorksLabs directly. Security concerns have a separate disclosure route.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:hello@codeworkslabs.dev?subject=CodeWorksLabs%20support">Email CodeWorksLabs <span>↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/security/">Security guidance</a></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="limitations"><strong>Support commitments are explicit.</strong><p>Public documentation, community discussion, and issue tracking do not create a guaranteed response time or a private support agreement. Any managed-service or contracted support boundary is documented separately.</p></section>
</Base>
